      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "For $v=\\sum_av^ae_a$ and $w=\\sum_bw^be_b$, bilinearity of $\\eta$ together with $\\eta(e_a,e_b)=\\operatorname{diag}(-1,1,1,1)_{ab}$ from [L1] give $\\eta(v,w)=-v^0w^0+v^1w^1+v^2w^2+v^3w^3$, hence $\\eta(v,v)=-(v^0)^2+\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert^2$, where $\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert^2=(v^1)^2+(v^2)^2+(v^3)^2=\\lVert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rVert_2^2$ by [L4]. The assignment $c(v):=(v^0,v^1,v^2,v^3)$ is a bijection $V\\to\\mathbb R^4$ by [L2]. By [L3] the timelike set is $T=\\{v:\\eta(v,v)<0\\}=\\{v:(v^0)^2>\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert^2\\}=\\{v:\\lvert v^0\\rvert>\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert\\}=T_+\\cup T_-$, because $\\lvert v^0\\rvert>\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert$ holds exactly when $v^0>\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert$ or $v^0<-\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert$.",
