          "claim": "The identity $\\operatorname{cl}(T_+)=\\{v:f(v)\\ge0\\}$ holds for the closure in the metric topology of [L9]: if $f(v)<0$, then every $u$ with $d(u,v)<-f(v)/2$ has $f(u)<0$ by the Lipschitz bound of step 2.3, so a ball about $v$ misses $T_+=\\{f>0\\}$ and $v\\notin\\operatorname{cl}(T_+)$; conversely, if $f(v)\\ge0$, then for every real $t>0$ the point $v+te_0$ has coordinates $(v^0+t,v^1,v^2,v^3)$ by [L2], hence $f(v+te_0)=f(v)+t>0$, so $v+te_0\\in T_+$ and $d(v+te_0,v)=t\\to0$. The same argument with $g(v)=-v^0-\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert$ gives $\\operatorname{cl}(T_-)=\\{v:g(v)\\ge0\\}$; in coordinates these are the displayed sets $\\{v:v^0\\ge\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert\\}$ and $\\{v:v^0\\le-\\lvert v_{\\mathrm{vec}}\\rvert\\}$.",
