          "claim": "By [L1], $x'^1=\\gamma(x^1-\\beta x^0)$ and $\\gamma>0$, so $x'^1=0$ holds exactly when $x^1=\\beta x^0$; the equations $x'^2=x^2$, $x'^3=x^3$ of [L1] show that the transverse coordinates are arbitrary constants, unchanged by the boost. Under the convention $x^0=ct$ of [L4], the locus is $x^1=\\beta ct$, that is, uniform motion along $e_1$ with coordinate velocity $\\mathrm dx^1/\\mathrm dt=\\beta c$.",
