          "quote": "A complex-linear functional $u:\\mathcal D(\\Omega)\\to\\mathbb C$ is a distribution if and only if, for every compact $K\\subseteq\\Omega$, there are an integer $m_K\\ge0$ and a finite constant $C_K\\ge0$ such that\n$$|u(\\varphi)|\\le C_K p_{m_K}(\\varphi)\\qquad(\\varphi\\in\\mathcal D_K).$$\nThe quantifiers are $\\forall K\\,\\exists(m_K,C_K)$; no simultaneous selection of witnesses is asserted or needed. The equivalence holds in ZF.",
