            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-vector-valued-derivative-and-integral",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "is **differentiable at $c$** when $\\lim_{x \\to c} q_{f,c}(x)$ exists in\n$\\mathbb{R}^{m}$, and then the **derivative** is\n\n$$f'(c) \\;:=\\; \\lim_{x\\to c} q_{f,c}(x) \\;\\in\\; \\mathbb{R}^{m}.$$\n\n**The notation denotes a single vector.**",
          "uses": [
