        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "lem-em-point-current-continuity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For $q\\in\\mathbb R$ and $\\psi\\in\\mathcal D(\\Omega)$ ([[def-test-function-space-d-of-an-open-set]]) define\n\n$$\\langle\\rho,\\psi\\rangle:=q\\int_I\\psi(z(t),t)\\,dt,\\qquad \\langle J,\\psi\\rangle:=q\\int_I z'(t)\\,\\psi(z(t),t)\\,dt,$$\n\nthe second integral being vector-valued with components $\\langle J_i,\\psi\\rangle=q\\int_Iz_i'(t)\\psi(z(t),t)\\,dt$. Then $\\rho$ and $J$ are distributions on $\\Omega$ ([[def-distribution]]) and, with the distributional derivative of [[def-distributional-derivative]],\n\n$$\\partial_t\\rho+\\operatorname{div}J=0\\qquad\\text{in }\\mathcal D'(\\Omega).$$\n\nProperness is automatic if $\\Omega=\\mathbb R^3\\times I$, and also if $I=\\mathbb R$.",
